  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Sidi bou Chaib</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A Roman settlement in Mauretania, mentioned in both Ptolemy and Pliny, has been associated with a site that was known as Sidi bou Cha\u00efb in the mid-20th century. That site is now in the territory of the modern Algerian town of Taougrite (colonial Paul-Robert), Chlef province.",
